{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on","id":1530670,"title":"What Beckett's Jyhad Diary plots were your favorite? Which would you followed up on?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-12T14:33:46-08:00","id":1530670,"title":"What Beckett's Jyhad Diary plots were your favorite? Which would you followed up on?","content":"What the title says.<br /> <br /> Talk about your favorite Beckett's Jyhad Diary bits and what you would have liked to have seen more of in a hypothetical future edition.<br /> <br /> + <b>House Carna</b> got some follow-up in V5 but I think that it deserved to be a lot more of a central figure than they got with the destruction of the Seven. Imagine if they were the Anarch alternative to the Camarilla Tremere.<br /> <br /> * I actually would have really enjoyed seeing how <b>Chicago </b>functioned under an oligarchy with no Prince. I also wanted to know if BJD was an in-universe document then did that mean Portia's masquerade was blown.<br /> <br /> + I really wanted to see who would be the new Regent of the Sabbat: <b>Lucita, Polonia, Jalan,</b> or perhaps some other dark horse figure like<b> Joseph Panders</b>.<br /> <br /> + The fact the<b> Tal'Mah'Ra </b>went from being a complete joke to something taking over Northern Africa and becoming a major sect in its own right.<br /> <br /> + <b>Ur-Shulgi </b>isn't a Beckett's Jyhad Diary plot but they seemed to be more interested in detailing that the Web of Knives wasn't the whole of the clan than the Revised version.<br /> <br /> + <b>Mary the Black, Michael, </b>and their search for the new member of the<b> Istanbul Trinity</b>.<br /> <br /> + <b>Vykos</b> regaining their free will after millennia.","signatur