rans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T16:50:23-08:00","id":1530686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1530674#post1530674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say I hated all of them and would rather provide my own plot points instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>What sort of plots would you have wanted instead if you were willing to spend money to purchase a book of plot points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T20:13:59-08:00","id":1530702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1530686#post1530686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sort of plots would you have wanted instead if you were willing to spend money to purchase a book of plot points?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here we go...<br /> <br /> First off, we start off with the setting assumptions of the Revised corebook. Not Revised as a whole, just the corebook. <br /> <br /> So the Gangrel are still in the Camarilla, there was no Week of Nightmares, Assamites are still Independent, it's still Clan Giovanni and not Hecata<br /> <br /> The Tremere Antitribbu are still extinct for some damn reason and the Sabbat still lost control of New York though. Thin-bloods aren't as prominent as they are in the canonical V5 though.<br /> <br /> Here's how I'd go about it...<br /> <br /> 1. Capone became Prince of Chicago with the explicit backing of Annabelle Triabell, Nicolai, and Tyler. Meanwhile, Kevin Jackson, Son, Ballard, Balthazar, Gordon Keaton, and Edward Neally all met Final Death throughout the remainder of the 90's and into the early 2000's. Meanwhile, the Anarchs of Chicago were able to fully expel Juggler from their ranks and a Triumvirate of Maldavis, Damien, and Gengis rule the Anarchs. Meanwhile, O'Leary, Tazmosius, Houdini, and a few others are currently MIA and Bret Stryker is now the Sheriff of Chicago at Annabelle's request.<br /> <br /> 2. The Sabbat crusade to take all of the East Coast largely ended in failure (only Atlanta was successfully conquered and even that was a Pyrrhic Victory) but the Camarilla were able to take all of New York and the Sabbat lost most of the Northeast in the ensuing counter-attacks. This has left the Sword of Caine in a weakened state, though they still remain a menace. As a result, the Sabbat began focusing more of their efforts outside of North America and bolstering the smaller domains they already have.<br /> <br /> The city of Charleston, West Virginia (and by extension all of the State of West Virginia) is the second-largest Sabbat domain that's east of the Mississippi, north of the Rio Grande, and south of the Saint Lawrence. In fact, Charleston has become increasingly prominent and prestigious among the Sabbat due to its potential as a staging point for a future crusade to retake the East Coast.<br /> <br /> 3. Victoria Ash continued to be a pop star but her career began to flag around 2002 or so. Now she's more of a &quot;Hey, remember me?&quot; punchline and is spoken of in the same breath as Mandy Moore, 98 Degrees, Vitamin C, B*Witched, and all the members of NSYNC not named Justin Timberlake.<br /> <br /> 4. Mictlantechtli was diablerized and met Final Death at the hands of some neonates from Chicago around 1992. Said neonates were instrumental in the War of Chicago and helping Capone stabilize his power base and securing alliances with Annabelle and Nicolai.<br /> <br /> 5. Juggler and Modius met Final Death in 2011. Alexander Danov left Gary shortly after the War of Chicago in 1993 and eventually made his way to Hunendora Castle. Michael is MIA, while Lucian, Alicia, and Evelyn Stephens all left Gary around 2000 or so. Lucian was recalled to New York, Alicia and Evelyn retreated further into Chicago and it's suspected that Evelyn suggested the idea of an Anarch Triumvirate<br /> <br /> 6. The events of Bloodlines happened with a female Tremere fledgling helping Maximilian Strauss take over the city of Los Angeles and the Ankaran Sarcophagus now in a warehouse somewhere.<br /> <br /> 7. Vykos met Final Death in 2004 at the hands of Caiaphas Smith. Jan Piertzoon also meets a similarly grisly end to an unknown assailant<br /> <br /> 8. The Final Death of Vykos (at the hands of a mortal hunter no less!), Giangaleazzo defecting to the Camarilla, the loss of the Tremere Antitribbu, and the failure of the East Coast Crusade have all forced the Sabbat into more defensive positions though rumors persist of a potential second crusade to take more territory in the Americas.<br /> <br /> 9. On December 31, 2009, Melinda Gailbraith mysteriously disappears. Nobody knows if she's met Final Death, is in Torpor, or just walked out. The very next night, Joseph Pander is called to Mexico City and is proclaimed the acting Regent, with the understanding that his position is supposed to be a temporary one.<br /> <br /> 10. In 2010, the Sabbat hold a grand convention in West Virginia with the provisional Regent, the Prisci, the Cardinals, and various elder Archbishops of note all meeting at the mansion of Sergei Von Bratovitch, the Tzimisce Archbishop of Charleston. There, they discuss the future of the Sect and make several sweeping changes. Lucita de Aragon arrives as a guest of honor as well, having rejoined the Sabbat in full.<br /> <br /> First off, they are shifting their blood war against the Camarilla into more of a cold war. Though they still will send threats to the Camarilla and Anarchs about a future crusade, it's all just a diversion while they work on a much grander plan, one jokingly nicknamed &quot;Operation Country Roads&quot; at the conference, but said jocular moniker ends up sticking anyway.<br /> <br /> A vote is held to determine the new permanent Regent and much to everyone's surprise, Joseph Pander is narrowly elected to be the new Regent, with Lucita being the deciding vote. His provisional figurehead title is now one of real substance. And from there, the new plan is to lead a much bigger and more meticulously planned crusade, one that is focused entirely on the Middle East, with their main focus being on taking out the Antediluvians. It will not be a mass exodus but instead an extended multi-step grand strategy and the first packs are deployed to the Levant on December 21st, 2012. <br /> <br /> 11. The first act of Operation Country Roads is a surprising success, with the Ashirra losing control of the cities of Mosul, Bethlehem, Aleppo, Tripoli, Beirut, and Amman while the Sabbat sustains minimal casualties (mostly shovelheads). Damascus falls exactly one year later with Carolina Velez, the disgraced former Archbishop of Montreal is now the Archbishop of Damascus.<br /> <br /> 12. Now we go into the Second Inqusition, AKA the one idea V5 had that had some genuine potential (even if it was botched badly in practice)<br /> <br /> The sheer bloodshed in the Middle East following the events of Operation Country Roads and the Sabbat's mounting successes in the Levant along with their continued depravity in the Americas ends up creating a lot of buzz online, with many videos of blatant Sabbat atrocities ending up on shock sites like LiveLeak. <br /> <br /> In 2014, Bob Schnoblin, using his CIA connections, is able to secure the formation of a federally commissioned joint task force comprised of civilian, military, and religious authorities to probe further into the chaos consuming the Middle East. He dies shortly after the commission is approved but he hand picks William Shephard of the FBI to be the new leader of the task force. <br /> <br /> This new task force comprised of the NSA, the FBI Special Affairs Department, the Department of Homeland Security, the US Army, and &quot;spiritual consultants&quot; (i.e. The Society of Leopold, and to a lesser extent, the Order of Saint George) and with their combined effort, they blow the Masquerade wide open. This doesn't get leaked to the general public, with operations against the Kindred being written off as &quot;counter-terrorist operations&quot;. <br /> <br /> Mithras is killed and London falls into chaos, but the attempts by the Second Inquisition to drone-strike the main Tremere chantry in Vienna fail due to the interference of Thaumaturgy. Marcus Vitel, Prince of DC, who narrowly resisted the Sabbat crusade and did all he could to prevent a Second Inquisiton, is killed at the hands of an elderly Sullivan Dane in 2017, but not before taking Dane down with him.<br /> <br /> The SI successfully eliminates all the Kindred in the wider Washington DC metropolitan area, causing the Camarilla leadership to have a collective &quot;OH SHIT!&quot; moment<br /> <br /> The SI focuses its efforts primarily on Camarilla and Anarch forces at home in the West, ironic given that the Sabbat were the Sect whose actions were the most directly responsible for its creation. However, the Sabbat do lose Atlanta due to SI efforts, allowing the Anarchs to take over once the dust settled.<br /> <br /> 13. Rumors of a Sixth Great Maelstrom and the demise of the Tal'mahe'Ra were greatly exaggerated. As the Second Inquisition tore through the West and Operation Country Roads continued unabated in the Middle East, the True Black Hand became more prevalent and active. <br /> <br /> 14. Sutekh is dead. Killed while he was still asleep in torpor. Set met Final Death in a mysterious and great explosion in Egypt. Nobody knows if it was the Sabbat, the Second Inquisition, the Tal'Mahe'Ra or something else entirely. The Followers of Set have become severely fractured as a clan. A splinter group calling themselves the Ministry of Set emerged in 2018, but was swiftly eradicated by the Tal'Mahe'Ra.<br /> <br /> 15. The Harbingers of Skulls leave the Sabbat and the Cappadocian Drenis leaves Transylvania. Drenis begins embracing many people and recruiting Thin-Bloods as an attempt to revive Clan Cappadocian. Sporting a goth style with Wiccan motifs and calling themselves the Hecata and join forces with the Harbingers and the Samedi, they try to directly attack the Giovanni estates in Venice but fail miserably, being wiped out to the very last one. Many Samedi refused the call to join up with the short-lived Hecata movement and survived.<br /> <br /> 16. Beckett is invited to Chicago by Rebekah the Monitor and is inducted into the Inconnu in 2021 and is told that something truly major, bigger than anything else in the history of the Kindred is about to happen very soon and he will play a major role in it<br /> <br /> 17. Menele awakened shortly after the death of Lodin and was convinced by Rebekah to forsake his war with Helena and instead join the Inconnu. Around the same time, the Children of Osiris and the seven surviving members of Clan Salubri joined the sect, becoming de facto sub-factions of them.<br /> <br /> These are just my personal ideas and I know you probably won't like them and neither will most V5/BJD fans but eh, I might as well share them anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T23:29:28-08:00","id":1530717,"title":"","content":"I liked the whole Southern Lords plotline. A bunch of Methuselahs ripped straight from feudalism, turned slave holders, all waking up together to impose their even more repressive practices on the modern day? Sound like great villains. And a perfect way for some up-and-coming Neonates to practice some Diablerie in a morally justified way, while not having to fight over who gets to do the eating. There's plenty to go around!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T12:56:30-08:00","id":1530839,"title":"","content":"That is lots of thought you put into your story ideas.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T13:08:34-08:00","id":1530840,"title":"","content":"Our plot points are limited to the following.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat as a whole has crumbled as they found out that they didn't even take down their antiduliveans and didn't even slow them down one bit. The news broke there fighting spirit and we see the Lasambra clan go either to the Camarilla or Anarch based on either age or mindset. The Tzimice have largely ignored sects and are rebuilding there traditions or creating new ones. There are a few packs operating but they are becoming fewer and fewer as hunters and the SI are taking them out.<br /> <br /> The Beckoning is happening, but nobody has a clue why the potent elders and ancients are feeling it and why some are not. The few that have returned seem either more potent or are strangely weaker.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquistion is still very much a threat and both the Camarilla and Anarchs are attempting to keep a lower profile &amp; find ways to protect themselves.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos are finding the death of there founder is still having strange effects on there disciplines and perhaps that the youngest and weakest might become mortal again and the few remaining older ones adapting to changes in there state.<br /> <br /> The Last Supper that created the Hecate happened and the Kindred in general are just thinking that there a new sect and not a altered clan.<br /> <br /> Those are a few of thing that we had in mind in our game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T18:58:27-08:00","id":1530860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on#post1530670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+ <b>House Carna</b> got some follow-up in V5 but I think that it deserved to be a lot more of a central figure than they got with the destruction of the Seven. Imagine if they were the Anarch alternative to the Camarilla Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted, and still want this in some form. Time permitting, I may do something short for the Vault, just to scratch that itch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on#post1530670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+ <b>Mary the Black, Michael, </b>and their search for the new member of the<b> Istanbul Trinity</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This bit of infernalism interests me less that whatever is going on in the ruins of Carthage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on#post1530670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+ <b>Vykos</b> regaining their free will after millennia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still want a follow up on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 02-15-2024, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T15:03:39-08:00","id":1531008,"title":"","content":"I quite liked Enoch possibly coming back and explaining the obvious about being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T10:34:36-08:00","id":1531024,"title":"","content":"Honestly the Drowned Legacies and the Laibon meeting were the only bits I really cared about.......but none of my Chronicles are set in the US or Europe so all that stuff is kinda just background noise for me.<br /> <br /> Would have like a bunch more Asian and Oceanian stuff in it but thems the breaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T10:36:14-08:00","id":1531025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531024#post1531024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the Drowned Legacies and the Laibon meeting were the only bits I really cared about.......but none of my Chronicles are set in the US or Europe so all that stuff is kinda just background noise for me.<br /> <br /> Would have like a bunch more Asian and Oceanian stuff in it but thems the breaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I couldn't get into the Laibon or Drowned Legacies because one of the things I had fun with at my home campaign's primary city was the Ventrue discovering their Clan already among the indigenous people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T17:42:06-08:00","id":1531043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531025#post1531025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, I couldn't get into the Laibon or Drowned Legacies because one of the things I had fun with at my home campaign's primary city was the Ventrue discovering their Clan already among the indigenous people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to dance around with that kind of thing, like you may have Vasantasena being disputed by a Tzimisce noble and a Malkavian holy man in 10th century India, or Inyanga as a shaman in 5th century southern Africa fighting &amp; being embraced by some Gangrel fleeing from trouble back in Egypt, but also Drowned Legacies, Laibon, Followers of Shesha in India, Bangladesh, Vietnam, Laos &amp; other southeast asian countries, Children of Susano-o in Japan, half-a-dozen lines of flesh-eating necromancers under different names &amp; supposed origins and some other stuff between canon, homebrew and deconstructed stuff.<br /> <br /> One of my games had the Dunsirn as &quot;Nagaraja&quot;, Pisanob as &quot;Samedi&quot;, Rossellini as Lamia and in fact many of the minor families as <b>rival</b> cabals/cults/lineages of necromancers fighting more than dealing with the Giovanni overall. Also, the Giovanni didn't really usurp the Cappadocians - oh, they probably caused the final death of a bunch of them, but the hunters did far worse (Cappadocians were the clan most severely hurt by the Inquisition, thanks to their own borderline monomania with christianism and its institutions, with Lasombra as a somewhat distant second), for wholy self-serving reasons that had no relation to lineage, that in fact they might <b>not </b>share.<br /> <br /> (Let's say i treat any direct ties between VtM and DAV continuity with a few pinches of salt....that and the DA setting also exists parallel to VtM as a psychic/spirit realm of sorts formed amidst the multifarious meanderings of the non-place known to many Malkavians, but not only to them, as the Cobweb)<br /> <br /> <br /> And truth be told i'm messing with the lines between clans, bloodlines, legacies and so on all the time, take <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagaraja_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">the Flesh-Eaters</a> for example<b>.</b><br /> For years i would have about four splinters - <b>Pishacha </b>in the Indian subcontinent and some neighboring countries; the <b>Ghul/Galla</b> in the middle east and much of the arab-speaking world; the <b>Dunsirn</b> family in the British Isles and parts of the Commonwealth as occasional allies of the Ventrue and foils to the Tremere &amp;/or Giovanni; and the <b>Nihilistics</b> cult/secret society in parts of Central and Eastern Europe.<br /> <br /> - Then in the middle of last year i heard about the name change of the &quot;Pure Ones&quot;/native american garou tribes in W5 - and decided that Wendigo <b>did</b> make an appropriate name for a bunch of grave-robbing, corpse-eating monsters, adding a native american one to the list.<br /> <br /> - And last week's discussion VDA20 Sarapion led me to do a binge read of the Mogadishu chapter of VDA20 Companion, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530149-vda20-sarapion?p=1530213#post1530213\">finding out</a> an interesting tidbit in the write-up of the Impundulu called Bantu that put the <b>Mla Watu</b> in a wholy different perspective, making them the sixth of the lot.... and from there i've been toying a bit with the Legacies as presented in KotEK, BJD &amp; VDA20 and the divergencies between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-02-2025, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T13:48:33-08:00","id":1531070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1530674#post1530674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say I hated all of them and would rather provide my own plot points instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't all bad in BJD proper, the writers did make a nice work at unearthing and updating many of the past citybooks plotlines plus delving into many of Revised era events, but in a more open-ended &quot;all this stuff is optional, use as is, ignore or rework as you prefer&quot; perspective, plus some bits from the novel and the two games.<br /> <br /> The fact some people in higher places would then jump from all the positive feedback into &quot;a bigger, more bold leap&quot; - and break their legs in the fall, badly, by not paying attention to how one lands, well, that's life. And Revised-era vitriol all over again, oh yeah, i know, but let me not digress too much. BJD on itself is far from bad, I enjoyed it as both fluff piece, compilation of the crazy from past editions, with some aim toward pointing optional alternate directions.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Carna's Rebellion is a funny case - 1 or 2 years back i got into BJD pretty much because of her little stunt in Milwaukee starting the whole trainwreck that is Beckett's misadventure through the whole book. The Book of Grave-War had already figured in some of my own games long before it and having her (instead of its better known translator, Mortius) breaking the bond and then going &quot;i wanna do Anarch Revolt 2.0, Tremere-only edition&quot; because of her many resentments &amp; emotional issues trumped over her sense i very much enjoy.<br /> <br /> Last year my idea of a chronicle was pretty much making her mess with Beckett and Vykos into the starting point as the PCs dealt with the sheer chaos of the Sabbat siege of Milwaukee, the maze of nonsensical intrigues of its kindred, the Lupines and a number of other subplots &amp; complications (Merick <b>still </b>is prince, though he has considerably cut on appearances since the 90's) while deciding if they stay to carve a niche, go into a Indiana Jones/Tomb Raider romp of their own alongside or against Beckett and who knows what else, among other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> But then i got in a Discord group, lots of random talk of fluff, editions, crazy ideas past &amp; present happened - and i ended up with a whole different chronicle concept &amp; group in my hands instead. Story is kind of centered on the &quot;False Caine&quot; plotline - or at least my own version of it, where no one found a mustache-twirling (female) setite behind the curtain and Karl Schreckt didn't get to defeat a 5th meth that, <i>even before power boost</i>, was three times his age already just because status quo is god. The Justicar called &quot;Caine&quot; an impostor and a threat to order and Traditions to be contained &amp; punished - and got <i><b>completely trashed into torpor</b></i> in front of dozens of kindred already quite awed with &quot;Caine&quot; for his troubles.<br /> <br /> Things only got weirder from there, as the princes either disappeared (or got disappeared with) and the hundreds of kindred from all over the world that moved into Berlin turned into the largest undead hippie/new age commune ever. And the headache would only spread as groups of kindred, some late responders to &quot;Caine's Beckoning&quot;, a lot of Malkavians (that were not called) gathering in neighboring cities to witness from a distance (that in particular had already been happening for weeks <i>before</i> Caine's arrival in Berlin) and groups of anarchs, noddists and occultists in general looking for some sort of opportunity or to prove someone wrong. The situation was hectic, the Camarilla attempted to retake the city - and completely failed in doing so. That one of the leaders of the personality cult was <i>another </i>Justicar, gone rogue and turned into one of the &quot;mad ancient&quot; confidantes, only made everything into more an epic embarassment for the Ivory Tower.<br /> <br /> <br /> And then a whole year later, it was all over. Just as suddenly as the spectacle started, it ended - some of the more diplomatically and philosophically adroit cultists (that included the aforementioned Justicar) had led negotiations between both sides, resulting in an armistice of sorts, &quot;Caine&quot; giving a few last words of counsel and support to his true witnesses and then leaving on its own for a personal pilgrimage and the whole his flock disbanding to all directions, individually or in groups, to follow personal visions of their own, exchange ideas and info.<br /> <br /> And sometimes start spiritual journeys/pilgrimages of their own, not infrequently tracking down all sorts of rumours of new Caine appearances, to follow in his steps, learn from them - and perhaps even exchange new revelations or ideas with the First of All when they do succeed in finding him.<br /> <br /> So ended the &quot;Third City Crisis&quot; and started the &quot;Witnesses of Caine&quot; proper as a somewhat unusual and iconoclastic noddist society back in the '90s. Los Angeles has been a particularly popular visiting spot since a series of incidents that would lead into the destruction of Prince Lacroix and a number of Sabbat, infernalists &amp; foreign undead causing trouble. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The PCs' coterie is strongly connected to the Witnesses, though technically only one of them is an actual full-fledged member, who was <b>literally </b>tracking down Caine/Kapaneus/Ankla Hotep/etc under the cover of his tour as a DJ (having sleeper buses and a roadie crew is very convenient to move the occasional kindred around too) when he would bump into not one but two kindred who actually met Caine in LA - one of them being a Gangrel reversed from centuries as a Gargoyle by the First, to boot - sort of recruited them, while also bumping into other peculiar kindred that sort of tagged along for all kinds of reasons.<br /> <br /> They also happen to presently be hunted by two different groups of Gargoyles with opposing religious manias (Heaven and Devil) and Dylan Bruce, who's after &quot;Dracula's Sword&quot; (actually the Sword of Nul, but try to convince the self-proclaimed &quot;childe of Dracula&quot; otherwise....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). Plus the Vukodlak - though technically Erik (the ex-Gargoyle) and sister Agnes (the Salubri warrior-nun) are really after freshly-awakened <b>Christoph's</b> steps, actually....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-08-2026, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T14:08:40-08:00","id":1531071,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> I will admit that V5 did negatively color my perception of BJD as I read the V5 corebook before reading BJD.<br /> <br /> With that said, how do you feel about my alternate plot points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T15:21:09-08:00","id":1531073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531071#post1531071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/\">Baaldam</a> I will admit that V5 did negatively color my perception of BJD as I read the V5 corebook before reading BJD.<br /> <br /> With that said, how do you feel about my alternate plot points?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are all fine and lots of nice reference nods here and there. The part about the many new additions to the Inconnu is fun, though in my own games the Children of Osiris are possibly even worse off than the &quot;vanilla&quot; Salubri. Chicago, Washington and London i tend to mostly avoid and not delve much into, each for its own reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Me i would have offed Vykos too were he not sort of a big part of the Milwaukee Siege - that i still want to throw my group into though the Gargoyles, Dylan &amp; Sword of Nul drama, among other bits keeps getting in the way - so he stays undead, just in case i do manage to get things rolling in that direction. But Sabbat controlling Washington? Hell, no, that would be ludricous even <i>without </i>Vykos in the lead. He rules in Detroit, that is possibly the thing closest to a fully Sabbat-controlled hellhole one might find in the USA - also, much closer to Milwaukee, a bonus in this context.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat crusade from Revised era happens, but in 2005 instead, parallel to the wake of Hurricane Katrina - basically <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2005_Atlantic_hurricane_season\" target=\"_blank\">that year's</a> hurricane season serves as the backdrop for &quot;Under a Blood Red Moon: Caribbean Edition&quot;, with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lisette_Vizquel\" target=\"_blank\">Vizquel </a>and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Don_Medina_Sidonia\" target=\"_blank\">Sidonia </a>- in place of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wendy_Wade\" target=\"_blank\">Wade </a>&amp; Rigaud from Chicago by Night - leading a takeover attempt of Cuba, and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ambrosio_Luis_Mon%C3%A7ada\" target=\"_blank\">Mon\u00e7ada</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lasombra#Angellis_Ater\" target=\"_blank\">Angellis Ater</a> as substitute for Black Spirals in trying to control/corrupt <a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jupiter_(WOD)#Totem\" target=\"_blank\">Jupiter</a> and through it weather, to bring about Mon\u00e7ada's own attempt at the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Ages:_Darkening_Sky\" target=\"_blank\">Cry That Slays Light</a> in the modern era.<br /> <br /> Cuba is not captured nor the &quot;Fanum&quot; wholy corrupted, but the damage is immense in several countries, the Sabbat gets a foothold in southern united states and parts of the Bible Belt, but it also backfires, as they end up rousing things in the Underworld that respond by crossing the Shroud and boosting the lines of the Harbingers of Skulls in Mexico and Central America.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh yeah, the Harbingers - in my continuity they have zero connection to the Cappadocians and are a problem to Giovanni in Latin America, but also the Tremere, Sabbat and <i>many</i> other groups besides. They are most probably a Drowned Legacy, or something even stranger between Risen, Spectre and Thin-Blood. Some whisper of Xibalba and/or Mictlantecuhtli....<br /> <br /> That combined with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Francisco_Domingo_de_Polonia\" target=\"_blank\">Polonia'</a>s move into infiltrating US intelligence and counter-terrorism apparell - something that happened <b>before</b> the Camarilla's recovery of New York, might be said and went in high-gear after 9/11 - and subverting parts of these toward striking a number of places in the Middle East, Central Asia &amp; North Africa, means the bizarre situation the Sabbat as a whole being wildly successful and stretched thin both in the last decade or so (chronicle is set in 2014 at the moment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-02-2025, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"