;, with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lisette_Vizquel\" target=\"_blank\">Vizquel </a>and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Don_Medina_Sidonia\" target=\"_blank\">Sidonia </a>- in place of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wendy_Wade\" target=\"_blank\">Wade </a>&amp; Rigaud from Chicago by Night - leading a takeover attempt of Cuba, and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ambrosio_Luis_Mon%C3%A7ada\" target=\"_blank\">Mon\u00e7ada</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lasombra#Angellis_Ater\" target=\"_blank\">Angellis Ater</a> as substitute for Black Spirals in trying to control/corrupt <a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jupiter_(WOD)#Totem\" target=\"_blank\">Jupiter</a> and through it weather.<br /> <br /> Cuba is not captured nor the &quot;Fanum&quot; wholy corrupted, but the damage is immense in several countries, the Sabbat gets a foothold in southern united states and parts of the Bible Belt, but it also backfires, as they end up rousing things in the Underworld that respond by crossing the Shroud and boosting the lines of the Harbingers of Skulls in Mexico and Central America.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh yeah, the Harbingers - in my continuity they have zero connection to the Cappadocians and are a problem to Giovanni in Latin America, but also the Tremere, Sabbat and many other groups besides. They are most probably a Drowned Legacy, or something even stranger between Risen, Spectre and Thin-Blood. Some whisper of Xibalba and/or Mictlantecuhtli....<br /> <br /> That combined with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Francisco_Domingo_de_Polonia\" target=\"_blank\">Polonia'</a>s move into infiltrating US intelligence and counter-terrorism apparell - something that happened <b>before</b> the Camarilla's recovery of New York, might be said and went in high-gear after 9/11 - and subverting parts of these toward striking a number of places in the Middle East, Central Asia &amp; North Africa, means the bizarre situation the Sabbat as a whole being wildly successful and stretched thin both in the last decade or so (chronicle is set in 2014 at the moment).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do like your ideas and I wonder how you feel about my ideas about the Convention of Charleston, and Operation Country Roads, where a previously beleaguered Sabbat gets a second wind and unexpectedly claps the Ashirra's cheeks throughout the 2010's?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T21:56:39-08:00","id":1531089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531076#post1531076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I do like your ideas and I wonder how you feel about my ideas about the Convention of Charleston, and Operation Country Roads, where a previously beleaguered Sabbat gets a second wind and unexpectedly claps the Ashirra's cheeks throughout the 2010's?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i loved those. Joseph Pander has been one of the more interesting figures in the bits of internal politics and history of the Sabbat as a sect and the fact he went mostly ignored for the whole of VtM first run felt like a huge disservice. Then comes <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Joseph_Pander\" target=\"_blank\">Rites of the Blood</a>, to change <i>everything </i>we thought we knew about the Panders as a movement and show Joseph in a whole new light in one ritual, that does not even get a level and all its ramifications (on an aside, it was through BJD, the dialogue between Beckett and Benezri, that i learned about the lore update/upgrade on the Panders). So, while i'm not a fan of the whole &quot;rock falls, Gallbraith dies&quot; subplot from Revised per se, seeing it solved with Joseph as impromptu Regent to <b><i>really </i></b>shake things up is awesome indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, in my Milwaukee plans he's also one of the major leaders in the siege - deeply to the frustration and distaste of Vykos, who has much less of a free hand than he would prefer due to constant crosschecking and interference from him, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dominique_Touraine\" target=\"_blank\">Dominique</a> (now a Salubri antitribu, much to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Adonai\" target=\"_blank\">Adonai</a>'s equal distaste - more on that later), Parovich (who clearly has some bizarre <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tal%27mahe%27Ra\" target=\"_blank\">agenda</a> but is the Sabbat's top grapevine into the city's happenings) and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dimitri\" target=\"_blank\">Dimitri </a>(actually Lasombra of the Amici Noctis in my games). They are all galling but Joseph is the worst of the lot, constantly questioning his decisions and keeping tabs on his motives. Vykos has no doubt the detestable upjumped rabble would attempt to topple him in the bat of an eyelash if he learned that Vykos' true aim is obtaining Carna's copy of the Book of Grave War.<br /> <br /> What is doubly ironic, since this distrust and rivalry between both Prisci also results in Vykos never learning Joseph Pander <i>already knows and possesses a copy of the book</i>, that indeed was a key component in devising the rite that breaks one blood's ties to their founders! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As an aside, my version of Joseph also thoroughfully detests Thin-bloods, what has led to him influencing the adoption of some <i>peculiarly conservative</i> policies within the sect and particularly this war campaign, in relation to them (also, my version of Milwaukee has become something of a duskborn refuge in the years between the &quot;Psychomachia killings&quot; and the Siege, for a number of reasons).<br /> <br /> [I have sort of tinkered with the idea of Thin-Bloods in my most recent game, partly inspired by BJD's sub-chapter on them in Anarch Freefall, coming up with some points of divergence - and conflict, as you can guess from my comment on Joseph's feelings on them, for example - from Caitiff, among other things]<br /> <br /> Plus, he might be actually kind of related to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Yaryan\" target=\"_blank\">someone</a> not exactly that far away from local events....<br /> <br /> <br /> Operation Country Roads is a good one too - truth be told, using the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gehenna_War\" target=\"_blank\">Gehenna War</a> to comment upon/explore the last two decades of chaos in many muslim countries is kind of a natural. Some people might take issue with that as culturally insensitive like hell <i>but action movies &amp; spy thrillers are among the most <b>anything</b>-insensitive popular genres ever anyway</i>, so whatever. Kudos to you.<br /> <br /> That said, my take of things is a little more pulverized in some ways, with thoroughfully Black Hand-infiltrated PMCs in Afghanistan and Iraq, Anarch cabals involved in all too many pies in the movements of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arab_Spring\" target=\"_blank\">Arab Spring</a>, a dizzying mess of factions on the nightmarish fighting spilling between Iraq, Syria and other neighnoring countries.<br /> <br /> Also, the Ashirra are more of a regional politico-religious kindred alliance restricted to the Arabian Peninsula proper (a good chunk of the Arab-speaking having formed ties to the Ivory Tower <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franco-Ottoman_alliance\" target=\"_blank\">thanks to Toreador diplomacy of centuries pas</a>t) and possible <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ashur\" target=\"_blank\">origins</a> quite <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Taft%C3%A2ni#Factions\" target=\"_blank\">unlike</a> their appearances might indicate....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-08-2026, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T08:03:54-08:00","id":1531115,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a><br /> <br /> Hi, I'm Travis and I'm 