oseph Pander <i>already knows and possesses a copy of the book</i>, that indeed was a key component in devising the rite that breaks one blood's ties to their founders! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As an aside, Joseph also thoroughfully detests Thin-bloods, what has led to him influencing the adoption of some <i>peculiarly conservative</i> policies within the sect and particularly this war campaign, in relation to them (also, my version of Milwaukee has become something of a duskborn refuge in the years between the &quot;Psychomachia killings&quot; and the Siege, for a number of reasons).<br /> <br /> [I have sort of tinkered with the idea of Thin-Bloods in my most recent game, partly inspired by BJD's sub-chapter on them in Anarch Freefall, coming up with some points of divergence - and conflict, as you can guess from my comment on Joseph's feelings on them, for example - among other things]<br /> <br /> Plus, he might be actually kind of related to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Yaryan\" target=\"_blank\">someone</a> not exactly that far away....<br /> <br /> <br /> Operation Country Roads is a good one too - truth be told, using the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gehenna_War\" target=\"_blank\">Gehenna War</a> to comment upon/explore the last two decades of chaos in many muslim countries is kind of a natural. Some people might take issue with that as culturally insensitive like hell <i>but action movies &amp; spy thrillers are among the most <b>anything</b>-insensitive popular genres ever anyway</i>, so whatever. Kudos to you.<br /> <br /> That said, my take of things is a little more pulverized in some ways, with thoroughfully Black Hand-infiltrated PMCs in Afghanistan and Iraq, Anarch cabals involved in all too many pies in the movements of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arab_Spring\" target=\"_blank\">Arab Spring</a>, a dizzying mess of factions on the nightmarish fighting spilling between Iraq, Syria and other neighnoring countries.<br /> <br /> Also, the Ashirra are more of a regional politico-religious kindred alliance restricted to the Arabian Peninsula proper (a good chunk of the Arab-speaking having formed ties to the Ivory Tower <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franco-Ottoman_alliance\" target=\"_blank\">thanks to Toreador diplomacy centuries ago</a>) and possible <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ashur\" target=\"_blank\">origins</a> quite <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Taft%C3%A2ni#Factions\" target=\"_blank\">unlike</a> their appearances might indicate....</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'm glad you like the ideas.<br /> <br /> My whole take with the idea of Operation Country Roads and the Sabbat going on a crusade to hunt down the Antediluvians and essentially BTFO'ing the Ashirra in the process was that while the strife in the Middle East during the 2010's was purely created by humans (just like in our world), vampires such as the Sabbat would gladly barnacle themselves to the chaos and exploit the fuck out of it for their own ulterior motives. Some might call it problematic but I honestly don't give a shit.<br /> <br /> Joseph Pander leading a grand crusade and actually winning was an idea I always liked, especially when paired with the state of West Virginia becoming a de facto second capital almost on par with Montreal in terms of importance to the 21st Century Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I also liked having the whole &quot;Clan Hecata&quot; bullshit from V5 get shut down quickly by the Giovanni in my alternate timeline. Drenis renounces the Inconnu, cliques up with the Harbingers of Skulls, half the Samedi, and a bunch of Caitiffs and Thin-Bloods before embracing a bunch of random goths and Wiccans to create &quot;Clan Hecata&quot; and avenge the Cappadocians, only for the entire Hecata movement to get wiped out in a single night by the Giovanni elders, with rumors of Augustus Giovanni himself personally waking up and laying the smackdown on Drenis and the Harbingers before groggily retreating back into the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T08:36:44-08:00","id":1531119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531115#post1531115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a><br /> <br /> Hi, I'm Travis and I'm a new addition to the moderation team. Apologies for the delay in addressing this, however, posts with high numbers of links are auto-flagged for moderation. Posting the same post repeatedly is spam, which also triggers moderation. We try to address moderation tasks in a timely fashion and ask you be patient and not spam the forum with multiple copies of the same post in the future.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25920_8.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25920\" data-vbnamecard=\"25920\">Matt Corleone</a> the same rule applies to replies. To avoid getting automodded when you quote a post with several links, please only quote the pertinent phrases and avoid the links as it will prevent this issue in the future. Please refrain from taking actions that ignore moderator warnings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T08:57:50-08:00","id":1531125,"title":"","content":"The cyclical Gehenna, by far was my most interested point in all this!<br /> <br /> Lucita becoming Regent-candidate I thought was out of left field<br /> The whole Ravnos bit was confusing and to me lead to nowhere interesting, same as Rasputin, Smiling Jack, and some similar<br /> <br /> It cyclical Gehenna gives new light to the War of Princes (or maybe the Anarch War). The whole Eternal Struggle, and it is even more terrifying than the original end-all apocalypse Gehenna idea. Cuz you know, it something that happened, and will happen, and hardly anyone knows/noticed it; the world keeps spinning, but all Kindred are affected. It is like instead of mortals hunting Kindred, or Kindred hunting Antediluvians, the Antediluvians themselves are hunting us, quietly, without an open war, but taking select targets one by one, or making bizarre (and more explicit) phenomena like the Week of Nightmares and the Beckoning. It is great for Horror! <br /> <br /> That for me was the richest aspect of BJD, and I'm very thankful how V5 synergized with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T16:39:04-08:00","id":1531151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531125#post1531125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cyclical Gehenna, by far was my most interested point in all this!</div> </div> </div> </div>That is something of a <b><i>very </i></b>old bit of hypothetical lore that i had sort of kept in my games and seeing it make a comeback to the limelight in V20 made me very happy indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531125#post1531125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucita becoming Regent-candidate I thought was out of left field</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Feels so very counter to her narrative of being one of the most visible &amp; active of the Lasombra Antitribu, not to mention antagonism toward her sire Mon\u00e7ada, that plays no small part in the previous. But well, her going Sabbat to at least a degree was a trainwreck that has been around since the novels, so the BJD writing team might as well give it something of a spin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531125#post1531125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole Ravnos bit was confusing and to me lead to nowhere interesting, same as Rasputin, Smiling Jack, and some similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you think the Ravnos bit was confusing, try to check the Revised era &amp; novels morass it was trying to respin some semblance of order from. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> No comments on Rasputin since it's one of the few chapters i haven't really read. Ok, maybe <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=16y1AkoZkmQ\" target=\"_blank\">one</a>.<br /> <br /> Smiling Jack was a pirate before he was an Anarch, or a vampire, for that matter. Do a Pirates of Caribbean marathon, read Pirate Utopias - and some news on Somali pirates or piracy in the Persian Gulf for a counterpoint/contrast - then all sorts of bizarre puzzle pieces will start fitting in on their own.<br /> <br /> (Also, where did he learn Thaumaturgy from - little possible hint: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mama_Lion\" target=\"_blank\">Mama</a> can be a honorific among practicioners of Voodoo and related traditions in both sides of the Atlantic &amp; beyond)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531125#post1531125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It cyclical Gehenna gives new light to the War of Princes (or maybe the Anarch War). The whole Eternal Struggle, and it is even more terrifying than the original end-all apocalypse Gehenna idea. Cuz you know, it something that happened, and will happen, and hardly anyone knows/noticed it; the world keeps spinning, but all Kindred are affected. It is like instead of mortals hunting Kindred, or Kindred hunting Antediluvians, the Antediluvians themselves are hunting us, quietly, without an open war, but taking select targets one by one, or making bizarre (and more explicit) phenomena like the Week of Nightmares and the Beckoning. It is great for Horror!<br /> <br /> That for me was the richest aspect of BJD, and I'm very thankful how V5 synergized with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games it gets worse in some small ways - there are hints the &quot;every Clan has an Antediluvian its own&quot; common assumption is at least partly incorrect, if not maliciously false - the Antediluvians <i>transcend</i> clan lines, their identities and actual numbers uncertain and evidence exist that some destroyed all their childer (or never embrace any), while others would generate several clans across the ages.<br /> <br /> Any vampire older than 2500 years is probably a past Gehenna escapee/survivor - and 50% chance of being from a completely alien lost clan and blatantly lying through word &amp; blood magic about what he or she truly is to play on contemporary kindred loyalties/sympathies. Puts a number of canon NPCs in a whole new light....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-26-2025, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T18:51:38-08:00","id":1531163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531151#post1531151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games it gets worse in some small ways - there are hints the &quot;every Clan has an Antediluvian its own&quot; common assumption is at least partly incorrect, if not maliciously false - the Antediluvians <i>transcend</i> clan lines, their identities and actual numbers uncertain and evidence exist that some destroyed all their childer (or never embrace any), while others would generate several clans across the ages.<br /> <br /> Any vampire older than 2500 years is probably a past Gehenna escapee/survivor - and 50% chance of being from a completely alien lost clan and blatantly lying through word &amp; blood magic about what he or she truly is to play on contemporary kindred loyalties/sympathies. Puts a number of canon NPCs in a whole new light....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm not a fan of the Cyclical Gehenna idea. But that is <i>really</i> cool.<br /> <br /> In some ways we kind of see evidence for &quot;The Antedeluvians created Clans multiple times&quot; in canon, if we squint.<br /> <br /> There's of course the Salubri and Assamites, who both have multiple castes with slightly different Disciplines, Weaknesses, and cultures. (To a lesser extent the Ravnos &quot;Jati&quot; could also fit here). In light of a Cyclical Gehenna, they may represent Clan recreations that were allowed to exist concurrently, survive, and most importantly <i>be known</i>. Kindred in-universe may only know them AS members of the same Clan, because their creators<i> permitted</i> it.<br /> <br /> Conversely, it's an established possibility that Saulot created the Baali (deliberately or accidently), and they got out of hand (again, deliberately or accidently). Modern Kindred know of them at all because Saulot turned the Salubri towards the objective of eradicating them, and then that extermination <i>failed</i>.<br /> <br /> How many times have Clans or Bloodlines come into existence, and the later purge was simply <i>more successful</i>?<br /> <br /> The &quot;True Brujah&quot; are another candidate for this process. Are they the &quot;original&quot; Brujah Clan, that escaped eradication? Or were they a new &quot;Clan&quot; Brujah made, that didn't work out?<br /> <br /> Or the Samedi. We don't really know where &quot;The Baron&quot; came from. He might have been a survivor of a &quot;Clan&quot; Cappadocius created and purged, that stuck around long enough to create more. (Cappadocius also points to another example of a potential Clan purge, with the Feast of Folly. Sure, the Ante allowed a bunch of his Clan to survive, but he didn't HAVE to. How many &quot;Feasts of Folly&quot; occurred in history, where their creators elected to destroy them utterly? How many ancient crypts in the world are full of the torpid bodies of trapped Vampires?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T22:06:18-08:00","id":1531175,"title":"","content":"Truth be told the matter of origins and provenance of kindred and their many lineages is one where i'm always in preference of monkeywrenchs than sticking to any canon - though to be fair, part of this is because i started in a time when the lore was between scant to non-existent, 4-5 clanbooks, and the two page intros for the Independents &amp; Sabbat clans and some bloodlines in the two PGs and ST Handbooks.<br /> <br /> Damn, the chapter on the Gaki in a World of Darkness or the appendix on the Bushi in Dark Alliance: Vancouver gave about as much info as you could scrounge on the Giovanni, Ravnos or Assamites, more in the case of the Gaki, they might count as almost Tzimisce-souleater level detailed! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, for every clan there was some sort of deep jyhad secret nemesis or legend like the True Brujah or Nictuku (or Salubri body-snatchers within the Tremere Pyramid's own ranks), sometimes putting even their origins in question. For every official bloodline i would throw in at least one or two groups with the same disciplines &amp; weakness but a whole different origin tale or cultural associations. Some of it i mentioned in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531043#post1531043\">a previous post</a>.<br /> <br /> Sometimes i would even cook up something ludricous for its &quot;canon shock value&quot;, like replacing Baba Yaga with Koshchei the Deathless as a 4th gen Samedi (!) in a Rage Across Russia-inspired game.<br /> <br /> Also Giovanni with no &quot;family merger&quot; policies (my version is far closer to the &quot;Great Family&quot; of Maharet in Queen of Damned in spirit), somewhat more dubious relations to the Cappadocians (or Lasombra, but i digress) - plus instead of allies/branches, the Dunsirn (Nagaraja), Pisanob (Samedi), Rosellini (Lamia) &amp; co as several nemeses of the Giovanni in the business, crime or necromantic arenas, when not all of those, at least on various degrees of &quot;regional&quot; level.<br /> <br /> Its all in finding the right niche to pull to derivate something, giving a little though to ramifications - and then seeing the players scamper willy-nilly to make sense of it all or find some way to exploit the discovery somehow to their advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-02-2025, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T23:39:44-08:00","id":1531176,"title":"","content":"In terms of cyclical Gehenna, it's important to note that in the 1e Corebook mentioned a 2300 year cycle which implied the antedeluvians devoured almost all their descendants at the end of these cycles, and that the last time this occurred was around Alexander the Great's wars 2300 years ago (setting up that sometime soon there would be another devouring). I believe the 2300 year cycle was inspired by the Book of Daniel whose 2300 day prophecy was though to be one day = one year, and this 2300 years.<br /> <br /> That would seem to be rejected in 2e and later renditions, but its interesting as an insight into the original thinking behind Gehenna. The idea of a cyclical Gehenna is not inherently against the VtM mythos. Personally I don't think there is an objection between recycling the concept of a cyclical Gehenna and a final Gehenna that results in an apocalyptic end times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T04:17:15-08:00","id":1531183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531176#post1531176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of cyclical Gehenna, it's important to note that in the 1e Corebook mentioned a 2300 year cycle which implied the antedeluvians devoured almost all their descendants at the end of these cycles, and that the last time this occurred was around Alexander the Great's wars 2300 years ago (setting up that sometime soon there would be another devouring). I believe the 2300 year cycle was inspired by the Book of Daniel whose 2300 day prophecy was though to be one day = one year, and this 2300 years.<br /> <br /> That would seem to be rejected in 2e and later renditions, but its interesting as an insight into the original thinking behind Gehenna. The idea of a cyclical Gehenna is not inherently against the VtM mythos. Personally I don't think there is an objection between recycling the concept of a cyclical Gehenna and a final Gehenna that results in an apocalyptic end times.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And with all legends, how much truth, literal or symbolic, there is can vary immensely depending on version or an individual's perspective.<br /> Not to mention inadvertently self-fulfilling prophecies...<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kohen#Name\" target=\"_blank\">a little something</a> to put a interesting spin of sorts on Beckett's (mostly forgotten by metaplot itself) &quot;tribal theory&quot; (attention to the arabic cognate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T13:02:58-08:00","id":1531211,"title":"","content":"A cyclical Genhenna is what the Beckoning is turning out to be as a culling of the clans by the anti's by taking a page from The Feast Of Folly that Cappy did to his clan in our game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-21-2024, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T14:47:21-08:00","id":1531217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531176#post1531176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would seem to be rejected in 2e and later renditions, but its interesting as an insight into the original thinking behind Gehenna. The idea of a cyclical Gehenna is not inherently against the VtM mythos. Personally I don't think there is an objection between recycling the concept of a cyclical Gehenna and a final Gehenna that results in an apocalyptic end times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. The stakes could have been raised either by the ever-increasing personal power of the antediluvians themselves (particularly if one follows the on-the-cusp-of-transcending-from-vampirism-into-godhood element of one of the Gehenna scenarios), or because mortal population and technology has grown so much since the last such event when nailed horseshoes and water wheels were state-of-the-art inventions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T06:10:54-08:00","id":1531349,"title":"","content":"The unholy trinity beneath Istanbul really stood out for me. Off the top of my head, it's the only love letter to Vampire: The Dark Ages, my favorite edition of the game, in the entire book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T07:08:48-08:00","id":1531354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531349#post1531349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The unholy trinity beneath Istanbul really stood out for me. Off the top of my head, it's the only love letter to Vampire: The Dark Ages, my favorite edition of the game, in the entire book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends if you count Christof I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T12:25:23-08:00","id":1531376,"title":"","content":"The book has several references to content from Jerusalem by Night, Fountains of Bright Crimson, Clanbook Cappadocian, etc. etc. So yep, we did go further than Constantinople by Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T20:08:13-08:00","id":1531405,"title":"","content":"This thread motivated me to start planning a V5 book on House Carna for the Vault. I'm working on a couple of other project before I get to it. But I will. And a lot of it will be driven by spite. Because that's just the way I roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T22:32:17-08:00","id":1531410,"title":"","content":"Saulot's past with the Wu Zao is referenced in one chapter as well, which slipped my mind earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T00:51:31-08:00","id":1531414,"title":"","content":"My favorite moments in the book:<br /> <br /> * Mark Decker hosting Beckett in the baseball field as an Elysium.<br /> <br /> * Marcus Vitel making his Doctor Doom-esque return.<br /> <br /> * Beckett's horrifying encounter with Helena.<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat Civil War meetings<br /> <br /> * The introduction of Maria Saldanova, Lucita's sister.<br /> <br /> * Christof and Ecaterina teaming back up.<br /> <br /> * Vykos getting the Dracon out of their brain and regaining free will for the first time in centuires.<br /> <br /> * The Assamites asking for asylum and the Tremere freaking the Hell out.<br /> <br /> * All of the Assamites briefly frenzying for Kindred blood.<br /> <br /> * The climax where all of the Kindred are digging for Enoch's coffin.<br /> <br /> * Hesha being stunned that the 2nd generation exists and what that means for his faith.<br /> <br /> * A bunch of Archons hiding in the coffin like a clown car.<br /> <br /> * LASOMBRA!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T09:09:45-08:00","id":1531428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531414#post1531414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite moments in the book:<br /> <br /> * Mark Decker hosting Beckett in the baseball field as an Elysium.<br /> <br /> * Marcus Vitel making his Doctor Doom-esque return.<br /> <br /> * Beckett's horrifying encounter with Helena.<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat Civil War meetings<br /> <br /> * The introduction of Maria Saldanova, Lucita's sister.<br /> <br /> * Christof and Ecaterina teaming back up.<br /> <br /> * Vykos getting the Dracon out of their brain and regaining free will for the first time in centuires.<br /> <br /> * The Assamites asking for asylum and the Tremere freaking the Hell out.<br /> <br /> * All of the Assamites briefly frenzying for Kindred blood.<br /> <br /> * The climax where all of the Kindred are digging for Enoch's coffin.<br /> <br /> * Hesha being stunned that the 2nd generation exists and what that means for his faith.<br /> <br /> * A bunch of Archons hiding in the coffin like a clown car.<br /> <br /> * LASOMBRA!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to toot my own horn, but Operation Country Roads blows away all of those plot points and I came up with that one in five minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts: