ckers for the godawful later metaplot and always have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-v20-becketts-jyhad-diary\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...ts-jyhad-diary</a><br /> <br /> The Kickstarter for it was made in 2016. V5 was created in 2018. BJD is from a place of love for the lore by Richard Thomas while V5 rebooted a massive chunk of the setting. Also, V20 had been moving away from metaplot agnoticism for awhile. Which was good because metaplot is awesome.<br /> <br /> I don't think we're going to agree on this, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T10:42:21-08:00","id":1531479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531436#post1531436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall it being walked back somewhat that breaking the curse was effortless on his part, but it's still impressive even if it took years and a lot of moving parts/blood sacrifices to arrange.<br /> <br /> That bit where Tegyrus shuts up the Tremere Justicar by outlining the Amr's speculation about exactly how the curse was cast in the first place is probably my favorite passage in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall that it was a minor ritual according to the clanbook where Ug-Shugi using his lineage as a source of power to break the curse and it with two thirds of that caste being from him. It's still quite impressive feat for a recently active ancient who wasn't at full power yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T12:33:29-08:00","id":1531482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531476#post1531476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, no.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-v20-becketts-jyhad-diary\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...ts-jyhad-diary</a><br /> <br /> The Kickstarter for it was made in 2016. V5 was created in 2018. BJD is from a place of love for the lore by Richard Thomas while V5 rebooted a massive chunk of the setting. Also, V20 had been moving away from metaplot agnoticism for awhile. Which was good because metaplot is awesome.<br /> <br /> I don't think we're going to agree on this, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we're not going to agree on that and just politely agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned, metaplot is awful and it ruined the setting, it was a tool for certain nameless devs to police the setting and take away elements they thought were &quot;badwrongfun&quot; and the fact that some of the more toxic elements of WoD fandom hold onto metaplot and the whole &quot;badwrongfun&quot; rhetoric as holy canon doesn't help either.<br /> <br /> As for your assessment of BJD, all I can say is I feel you are wrong. V20 only started moving away from metaplot agnosticism near the very end (not counting the BNS LARP stuff) and it was part of a move towards what was essentially proto-V5.<br /> <br /> This was in preparation for an aborted &quot;V4&quot; from Onyx Path that resumed the metaplot, and that was like a proto-V5. There was also a lot of smug and pretentious semantics arguments about how V20 wasn't &quot;really&quot; a fourth edition because it was metaplot agnostic.<br /> <br /> There were quite a few V20 fans who were pissed at this announced &quot;V4&quot; and a shift away from metaplot agnosticism. Then Paradox swooped in and used this Onyx Path V4 as the springboard for what would become V5. Parawolf also did the only good decisions in their entire history of owning the WoD IP, they created the Storytellers Vault and also officially recognized V20 as the fourth edition of Vampire and threw away Onyx Path's semantics games regarding V20.<br /> <br /> BJD was essentially a V5 book in V20 trade dress, even if it didn't realize it fully. The proposed Onyx Path V4 was merely the dress rehearsal for V5, the Chainmail to V5's White Box D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 02-25-2024, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T00:27:12-08:00","id":1531495,"title":"","content":"The only thing BJD and v5 really have in common are attempts to walk forward the metaplot, so if you prefer street-level games and hate global/sect developments then I can understand why they would appear to be so connected. That doesn't make BJD as heinous as some of the changes that v5 made though, it still attempted to follow storylines set up in previous books which is one thing v5 isn't very worried about.<br /> <br /> Saying metaplot ruined the setting is kind of a dubious statement as 1. you don't have to follow the canon in your games and 2. its the only way to further develop the setting after so many v20 side books had already been made. If not a single plot point that BJD offered managed to pique your interest then that says more about your standards than it does about the book's quality, imo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T05:40:05-08:00","id":1531507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531479#post1531479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that it was a minor ritual according to the clanbook where Ug-Shugi using his lineage as a source of power to break the curse and it with two thirds of that caste being from him. It's still quite impressive feat for a recently active ancient who wasn't at full power yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see it being easy work for Ur-Shulgi. BJD says the Tremere ritual only worked because the Eldest consented on behalf of the entire clan. When the Shepherd awoke, he could presumably un-consent and take the clan with him. The ritual may have been the equivalent of tearing up the old contract or using his power of veto to negate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T06:33:09-08:00","id":1531508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>abugintherug</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531495#post1531495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing BJD and v5 really have in common are attempts to walk forward the metaplot, so if you prefer street-level games and hate global/sect developments then I can understand why they would appear to be so connected. That doesn't make BJD as heinous as some of the changes that v5 made though, it still attempted to follow storylines set up in previous books which is one thing v5 isn't very worried about.<br /> <br /> Saying metaplot ruined the setting is kind of a dubious statement as 1. you don't have to follow the canon in your games and 2. its the only way to further develop the setting after so many v20 side books had already been made. If not a single plot point that BJD offered managed to pique your interest then that says more about your standards than it does about the book's quality, imo</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 made the metaplot and the mechanics damn near inseparable, which is why I don't use it. I stick to older editions. So that's not the issue.<br /> <br /> The issue I have is that the specific WoD metaplot was horrible and the way WoD uses its metaplot has always been bad. It was used as a way to try and force a thematic purism upon people, and V5 was merely the apotheosis of what certain past WoD developers had been wanting to do for years, to purge the &quot;badwrongfun&quot;. So yeah, the metaplot helped ruin WoD as a setting IMHO. Unironically, give me Alien Hunger, Chaos Factor, and Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand over Beckett's Jyhad Diary or Time of Thin Blood or any V5 book ever.<br /> <br /> So I say fuck V5, fuck the metaplot, fuck BJD, fuck &quot;street level&quot; angst, and fuck &quot;true art personal horror&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 02-26-2024, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T06:50:32-08:00","id":1531510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531508#post1531508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 made the metaplot and the mechanics damn near inseparable, which is why I don't use it. I stick to older editions. So that's not the issue.<br /> <br /> The issue I have is that the specific WoD metaplot was horrible and the way WoD uses its metaplot has always been bad. It was used as a way to try and force a thematic purism upon people, and V5 was merely the apotheosis of what certain past WoD developers had been wanting to do for years, to purge the &quot;badwrongfun&quot;. So yeah, the metaplot helped ruin WoD as a setting IMHO. Unironically, give me Alien Hunger, Chaos Factor, and Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand over Beckett's Jyhad Diary or Time of Thin Blood or any V5 book ever.<br /> <br /> So I say fuck V5, fuck the metaplot, fuck BJD, fuck &quot;street level&quot; angst, and fuck &quot;true art personal horror&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am really confused by your association of Beckett's Jyhad Diary with any of this because it was a celebration of every single metaplot from 1st Edition to Revised in all their silly and serious glory simultaneously.<br /> <br /> You had Helena and Milwaukee next to the Baali next to Anathema.<br /> <br /> It is absolutely not any form of gatekeeping but a pinata of many candies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T07:29:16-08:00","id":1531512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531510#post1531510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am really confused by your association of Beckett's Jyhad Diary with any of this because it was a celebration of every single metaplot from 1st Edition to Revised in all their silly and serious glory simultaneously.<br /> <br /> You had Helena and Milwaukee next to the Baali next to Anathema.<br /> <br /> It is absolutely not any form of gatekeeping but a pinata of many candies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that BJD was meant to revive the metaplot as a whole and to become a springboard for OPP V4 (and later V5) just left a bad taste in my mouth. It's kinda hard to explain but something about BJD just put me off and I'm not sure how else to explain it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T07:56:09-08:00","id":1531515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531512#post1531512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that BJD was meant to revive the metaplot as a whole and to become a springboard for OPP V4 (and later V5) just left a bad taste in my mouth. It's kinda hard to explain but something about BJD just put me off and I'm not sure how else to explain it</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand if metaplot is something you just don't want anything to do with. It makes perfect sense and isn't for everyone.<br /> <br /> Many people like the &quot;metaplot agnoticism&quot; of V20.<br /> <br /> But I guess I've always found it something I could use as springboards for ideas and games. I feel like BJD was really the best way to handle it as all of the metaplot is POTENTIALLY happening but none of the guns really fire until the ST says they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T09:00:07-08:00","id":1531523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531508#post1531508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 made the metaplot and the mechanics damn near inseparable, which is why I don't use it. I stick to older editions. So that's not the issue.<br /> <br /> The issue I have is that the specific WoD metaplot was horrible and the way WoD uses its metaplot has always been bad. It was used as a way to try and force a thematic purism upon people, and V5 was merely the apotheosis of what certain past WoD developers had been wanting to do for years, to purge the &quot;badwrongfun&quot;. So yeah, the metaplot helped ruin WoD as a setting IMHO. Unironically, give me Alien Hunger, Chaos Factor, and Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand over Beckett's Jyhad Diary or Time of Thin Blood or any V5 book ever.<br /> <br /> So I say fuck V5, fuck the metaplot, fuck BJD, fuck &quot;street level&quot; angst, and fuck &quot;true art personal horror&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Please ease up - you can state your opinion without running down the creators and fans who enjoy all of those things, and you can do it without advancing pet theories about V4 and V5 that are not how things were intended or happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T09:02:37-08:00","id":1531524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531515#post1531515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand if metaplot is something you just don't want anything to do with. It makes perfect sense and isn't for everyone.<br /> <br /> Many people like the &quot;metaplot agnoticism&quot; of V20.<br /> <br /> But I guess I've always found it something I could use as springboards for ideas and games. I feel like BJD was really the best way to handle it as all of the metaplot is POTENTIALLY happening but none of the guns really fire until the ST says they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely understandable and yeah, I liked the metaplot agnostic approach of V20 the most.<br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of the Andrew Greenburg era of Vampire (1991-1994) as that was honestly an underrated and overhated era for VTM and WoD as a whole. For as much flack as the modern fanbase gives the Greenburg era, that was arguably the era of Vampire's greatest success and cultural relevance.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of all that angsty &quot;Woe is me! I'm such a monster!&quot; trad goth arthouse hipster stuff.<br /> <br /> Gimme the trenchcoats, katanas, &quot;Supers With Fangs&quot;, heavy metal mall goth attitude, and general &quot;badwrongfun&quot; instead.<br /> <br /> The best part about V20 and the Greenburg Era was that you could have both styles and often, both styles were mixed together in official sources to boot.<br /> <br /> You didn't have this false dichotomy of &quot;True Art Personal Horror vs. Supers With Fangs Badwrongfun&quot; that certain elements of the fanbase and certain nameless former devs tried to push from Revised onward. Though at least in Revised, they still gave you the tools for badwrongfun even as the text in some books chided you for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 02-26-2024, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T09:07:07-08:00","id":1531527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531523#post1531523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please ease up - you can state your opinion without running down the creators and fans who enjoy all of those things, and you can do it without advancing pet theories about V4 and V5 that are not how things were intended or happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that, I got a little too worked up there.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with &quot;true art personal horror&quot; having fans and I believe that it also has its place at the gaming table, I just get irked by some of the more toxic WoD fans who unironically believe in &quot;badwrongfun&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 02-26-2024, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T13:53:50-08:00","id":1531541,"title":"","content":"I personally thought that the Metaplot was just a outline to work from and you could put your own spin on it and that you decide what road to take with it as I mentioned some of the plot points we have in our games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-26-2024, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T17:10:09-08:00","id":1531566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531541#post1531541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally thought that the Metaplot was just a outline to work from and you could put your own spin on it and that you decide what road to take with it as I mentioned some of the plot points we have in our games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metaplot came in two varieties:<br /> <br /> * Updates to the setting to fit new rules, bloodlines, and so on.<br /> <br /> * Just random screwiness from White Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T12:48:18-08:00","id":1531694,"title":"","content":"I can just picture the signature characters in the setting asking themselves that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T21:56:53-07:00","id":1533504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531527#post1531527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry about that, I got a little too worked up there.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with &quot;true art personal horror&quot; having fans and I believe that it also has its place at the gaming table, I just get irked by some of the more toxic WoD fans who unironically believe in &quot;badwrongfun&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy, you should have seen how bad i could go on it back in the late '90s and turn of millenium with the Year of the Lotus and Revised Era stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531541#post1531541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally thought that the Metaplot was just a outline to work from and you could put your own spin on it and that you decide what road to take with it as I mentioned some of the plot points we have in our games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, it is. But as CTPhipps pointed out, some metaplot events can be one book or limited book arc things (Under a Blood Red Moon &amp; 2e Chicago, Giovanni or Transylvania Chronicles) that one might even be unaware exists if not following that particular niche. Meanwhile, you have the wide book/new game line arcs (Year of the Lotus) or edition update metaplot arcs, that can be considerably more pervasive in how they spread over everything and can be that much harder to ignore without outright forsaking the setting for a few years.<br /> <br /> It can also make interactions with players while trying to make new groups a little more convoluted, as one never knows beforehand if they are quite as in synch on their lore, interests &amp; preferences as they think. Oh yeah, that can get entertaining to manage, speaking from experience.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T12:19:34-07:00","id":1533525,"title":"","content":"So what things did you do in your games Baaldam that pushed against the lore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T14:32:13-07:00","id":1533574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531566#post1531566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Metaplot came in two varieties:<br /> <br /> * Updates to the setting to fit new rules, bloodlines, and so on.<br /> <br /> * Just random screwiness from White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Iirc they already updated the Metaplot in the V20 compendium by saying how Vampires act 2011 with the internet and this new Occupy Wallstreet Movement. Personally those where part of the &quot;good&quot; Metaplot which updates the setting.<br /> About the BJD Metaplots the two Metaplots that really captivated me where the one about House Carna and the one about the thinbloods.<br /> Especially the one about Gen 16 and the Dhampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T16:37:59-07:00","id":1533581,"title":"","content":"I'm liking the Beckoning as it's shaking up the power structure of Kindred society and we are seeing younger members making a play for positions of power and influence. Like Kevin Jackson using the conflicts in Chicago to claim the Prince spot despite his young age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T13:25:20-07:00","id":1533637,"title":"","content":"I liked it a lot, but ended up disregarding a lot also. Also, BJD inspired my boyfriend and i to make a shared-plot for London, in which Roger de Candem is aware much more early about Monthy Coven and is now in a civil war with Lady <b> Anne Bowesley</b>, using the Troubles as a form of fighting the power of Bowesley while trying to fully awake the potential of Mithras inside the body of Monty. Eventually Candem and Gestalted Mithras will win, with the Mithraic Misteries and Mithras as a whole becoming more powerful, and when the S.I attacks in 201X, Mithras isn't killed, only send to torpor, and kinda that Candem is making a plan to take the city of New York as a &quot;New Rome&quot; for Mithras","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T05:50:05-07:00","id":1533692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531354#post1531354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends if you count Christof I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. 2 of the PCs in my current chronicle are directly connected to his story and would seem familiar (and yet not) to those who played Redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T22:35:02-07:00","id":1536928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1531508#post1531508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 made the metaplot and the mechanics damn near inseparable, which is why I don't use it. I stick to older editions. So that's not the issue.<br /> <br /> The issue I have is that the specific WoD metaplot was horrible and the way WoD uses its metaplot has always been bad. It was used as a way to try and force a thematic purism upon people, and V5 was merely the apotheosis of what certain past WoD developers had been wanting to do for years, to purge the &quot;badwrongfun&quot;. So yeah, the metaplot helped ruin WoD as a setting IMHO. Unironically, give me Alien Hunger, Chaos Factor, and Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand over Beckett's Jyhad Diary or Time of Thin Blood or any V5 book ever.<br /> <br /> So I say fuck V5, fuck the metaplot, fuck BJD, fuck &quot;street level&quot; angst, and fuck &quot;true art personal horror&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. The metaplot, and the signature characters for The Clans, has always been terrible. The main one I extremely dislike seems to the the fan's favorite: Beckett. It seems the consensus at White Wolf, and now beyond, that he should be the 90's edgelord wetdream. Mainly. a snarky contrarian, sarcastic asshole, who should be immediately destroyed for being a smartass, but somehow escapes via Deus Vampex. Alan Moore's Constantine. But no, he's &quot;BADASS...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","user":"Illuminostro","date":". 06-08-2024, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:48:15-07:00","id":1537002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1536928#post1536928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you. The metaplot, and the signature characters for The Clans, has always been terrible. The main one I extremely dislike seems to the the fan's favorite: Beckett. It seems the consensus at White Wolf, and now beyond, that he should be the 90's edgelord wetdream. Mainly. a snarky contrarian, sarcastic asshole, who should be immediately destroyed for being a smartass, but somehow escapes via Deus Vampex. Alan Moore's Constantine. But no, he's &quot;BADASS...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Beckett has never been any sort of badass. He's a scholar not a warrior.<br /> <br /> He is, however, snide and his attempts to be snarky get a Blood Hunt on him by Hardestadt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:51:16-07:00","id":1537004,"title":"","content":"Beckett was more of a scholary bent in the Gehenna novel from what I could recall and had Caine more or less protecting him and before that it was Lucita or Antaole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:55:47-07:00","id":1537006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530670-what-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-plots-were-your-favorite-which-would-you-followed-up-on?p=1537004#post1537004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beckett was more of a scholary bent in the Gehenna novel from what I could recall and had Caine more or less protecting him and before that it was Lucita or Antaole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Beckett's snark was tolerated because he's an Elder and useful right up until he failed to read the room with Hardestadt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=